agent-ops task task-2acd8b8f-6a76-462e-ae73-09fbfb5fc139: Office resident staff: QA, two reviewers, integrator
intent: Each room gets resident staff besides the engineer: QA for verify, two reviewers for the two review rounds, an integrator for worktree finish. They rest in the lobby and walk to their station while their real process runs, recorded by a display-only activity record. Subtask A writes and reads the records; subtask B draws the staff.
criteria:
- staff-integrate: A verify, review or finish activity recorded for a session makes the matching staff member in that session's room walk from the lobby to their station, and back when it ends; a client test drives a verify and a review through a snapshot.
- no-slot-rooms: The Office no longer creates separate review-slot rooms; every running review appears inside the room it belongs to or in a temporary room named after its task; a test checks both.
  agent-ops task task-8c7c6499-538a-492c-9360-9559b06d5e12: Staff A: activity records
  intent: A small office activity module writes, updates and removes display-only activity records under the git common dir for verify, review (with targets and round via a new onRound callback on createReviewExecutor) and worktree finish; every write is fail-open and allowlisted. collect.ts reads live records and attaches them to rooms by session, task or worktree path, giving unmatched ones a temporary room; standalone review-slot rooms go away.
  criteria:
  - record-lifecycle: verify, review and worktree finish each write <git common dir>/agent-ops/office-activity/<kind>-<pid>-<n>.json (mode 0600; n counts records within one process) when they start, holding only kind, pid, root, startedAt and, when known, taskId, sessionId, worktree, and for review the planned targets, current round and target; they remove it when they end, whether they pass, fail or throw. Tests cover a helper round trip and a verify command run.
  - fail-open: A failure to write, update or remove an activity record never changes the command's result or throws; a test with an unwritable activity directory runs verify to its normal result.
  - review-rounds: createReviewExecutor calls an onRound callback with round 1 and its target before the first round and round 2 and its target before the adversarial round, and the review activity record follows it; a test with a fake runner checks both calls and the record.
  - office-read: The Office reads activity records, ignores malformed ones and those whose pid is no longer alive, and attaches each to the room with the same session id, else the same task id, else a worktree whose path equals its root; one that matches nothing gets a temporary room named after its task. A collect/snapshot test covers each match and a dead pid.
  agent-ops task task-3a6984d4-8ef2-48d6-8ca2-a9d866bae0d0: Staff B: resident staff in the rooms
  intent: Art gains QA and integrator clothing; the layout gains lobby rest spots and staff stations; the client places resident QA, two reviewers and an integrator in every room, walks them between lobby and station from the activity records, shows busy and result bubbles, swaps reviewers per round and keeps the engineer at the cubicle during verify, review and integrate.
  criteria:
  - resident-staff: Every session or run room has a resident QA, two reviewers and an integrator who rest at lobby spots while idle; the engineer works in planning or implementing and sits at the cubicle while the room is in verifying, reviewing or integrating. A client test checks the idle roster and the engineer's place.
  - walk-to-work: When a verify or finish activity starts, QA or the integrator walks from the lobby to the test bench or sorting table with a busy bubble; when it ends they walk back showing a check or cross taken from the snapshot result, which fades after about ten seconds. A client test checks the walk, the busy bubble and the result bubble.
  - two-reviewers: During a review both reviewers walk to the review room: in round 1 reviewer A works at the desk while B waits in an armchair, in round 2 they swap; nameplates use the activity's targets, else the newest report's, else A and B. A client test checks both rounds and the names.
  - staff-clothes: QA wears a light lab coat and the integrator khaki; both role palettes are distinct from the others and from the alert red. An art test checks it.
  - staff-reduced-motion: Under prefers-reduced-motion staff jump straight between lobby and station and result bubbles do not animate; a client test checks it.
